and 2-3 sequence motifs (e.g., zinc finger, catalytic triad). Each property is measured by a cheap, automated evaluator: DSSP/ESMFold for structure, biopython for GRAVY/MW, a linear probe or fine-tuned head for thermostability, regex/HMMER for motifs.\n2) SOLO CALIBRATION: For each feature, sweep steering strength and record property gain vs. Validity Budget (pseudo-perplexity, ESMFold pLDDT, naturalness). Establish per-feature effective operating range.\n3) COMPOSITIONALITY TEST (core): For all property PAIRS and a set of TRIPLES, co-steer at each feature's calibrated strength. Compute Interference Score = (solo property gain - co-steered property gain)/solo gain, for each property in the combination. Compare three methods: (a) additive SAE-feature steering, (b) raw activation-vector steering (difference-of-means directions), (c) Gram-Schmidt orthogonalized SAE-feature directions. Metrics: mean/worst-case Interference, joint success rate (all constraints satisfied above threshold), validity retention, sequence diversity and novelty.\n4) PREDICTORS OF STEERABILITY: For each feature compute (i) interpretability/concept-correlation score, (ii) causal-effect magnitude (property change per unit steer), (iii) monosemanticity under ablation, (iv) Jacobian/decoder-direction cosine alignment with other features. Regress compositional steerability (1 - interference) on these; test whether interpretability score is predictive vs. causal-effect magnitude. Report correlations and an ablation.\n5) INTERFERENCE STRUCTURE: Build a feature-feature interference matrix; test whether interference correlates with decoder-direction cosine similarity (predicting a simple geometric fix: pre-orthogonalize colliding features). Validate the orthogonalization fix in step 3c.\n6) GENERALIZATION: Repeat a reduced protocol on an RNA language model (RiNALMo/SAE-RNA) with 2-3 properties to test cross-domain transfer of the compositionality principle.\nEVALUATION METRICS: joint constraint satisfaction rate, per-property Interference Score, Validity Budget, ESMFold pLDDT, pseudo-perplexity, diversity/novelty, and predictive R^2 of steerability regressors.", 'Risk Factors and Limitations': '1) Property evaluators (structure/thermostability predictors) are imperfect proxies for wet-lab truth; conclusions are about in-silico controllability, not experimentally validated function. 2) Compositionality may be trivially poor if all chosen features live in a low-dimensional subspace; we mitigate by selecting features spanning diverse concept types and reporting the interference matrix. 3) SAE quality and layer choice could confound results; we control by comparing multiple SAE architectures (TopK, Matryoshka) and model sizes. 4) The predictive-regression analysis could be underpowered if the feature bank is small; we mitigate by including tens of features across properties. 5) Orthogonalization fix may reduce interpretability of steered directions, a tradeoff we will quantify rather than assume away.'}

