uction/interpretability sanity metrics.", 'Risk Factors and Limitations': "1) Requires generators with accessible per-step activations; if a target model's diffusion process is not easily instrumented we substitute alternatives, limiting generality to instrumentable models. 2) In-silico evaluators (ESMFold, DSSP, RDKit) are proxies for wet-lab function; claims concern model-internal causal timing and controllability, not experimental viability. 3) Causal windows may be entangled with steering strength; we sweep strength within each window and report timing effects controlling for strength. 4) Temporally-shared SAEs may blur timestep-specific features; we mitigate with temporally-conditioned SAEs and report differences. 5) The stratification hypothesis could fail (some fine properties decided early); a null or reversed result is still an informative, publishable characterization. 6) Feature-property linkage relies on concept-correlation, which can be non-causal; the sliding-window clamp is itself the causal test, so we treat correlation only as a candidate-selection step. 7) Efficiency gains depend on how much of the trajectory the causal window occupies; if windows are broad, savings shrink—this is directly quantified rather than assumed."}

